            "review_text": "TravelingAussiegirl\nMelbourne, Australia33 contributions\n0\nSweet little place but hard to find\nJul 2019 • Family\nNice little find in the middle of the city. Beautiful decor, cool and clean. Nice selection of cakes and extensive selection of tea! \n\nOnce you choose your tea you choose your cup and saucer- nice touch.\n\nFor a teapot of tea and 2 cakes you are looking at 340,000 VND/$20 AUD so mid range. \n\nCakes were nice and the tea is tea leaves as you would expect so lovely. \n\nBUT this place is near impossible to find. Best to ask them directly how to and remember to ask for floor number!! Or I’ll tell you! The entrance is between 2 shops in a non descriptive dark and dirty walkway. Then you have to pay the elevator guy to actually use the elevator. He didn’t know the floor we needed to get off but a local told us level 2. We get off just discover it’s not on 2! So we proceeded to walk up stairs (dirty) to find them! Lucky for us it was in level 4 and not higher. \n\nSo you can either pay the guy 3,000 VND per person (and shops don’t refund unlike the sign will tell you) to use the elevator or just walk up to level 4.\nRead more\nWritten July 16, 2019",
